Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-24
Subject: Guard tai_label\s tasmlabel narrowing casts during PPU load/deref
License: expat

`compiler/aasmtai.pas` narrows `tai_label.l` from the generic
`tasmsymbol` base type in two places:

  l := tasmlabel(ppufile.getasmsymbol);
  objectlibrary.DerefAsmsymbol(tasmsymbol(l));

Both paths can leave `l` pointing at a plain `tasmsymbol`. In the
bootstrap subset these old-style casts lower to reinterpreting views,
so the later `tai_label(hp).l.is_used` path in `aggas` ends up making
a member call through a `tasmlabel`-typed reference whose dynamic
object is only a base `tasmsymbol`. UBSan reports that immediately
during the stage-2 compiler build.

This is the same cleanup style as the other FPC 2 source guards:
perform the runtime type test first, narrow only after that, and fail
loudly if the PPU stream violates the expected invariant.

--- a/compiler/aasmtai.pas
+++ b/compiler/aasmtai.pas
@@ -1446,9 +1446,15 @@
 
 
     constructor tai_label.ppuload(t:taitype;ppufile:tcompilerppufile);
+      var
+        s : tasmsymbol;
       begin
         inherited ppuload(t,ppufile);
-        l:=tasmlabel(ppufile.getasmsymbol);
+        s:=ppufile.getasmsymbol;
+        if assigned(s) and (s is tasmlabel) then
+          l:=tasmlabel(s)
+        else
+          internalerror(2005050501);
         is_global:=boolean(ppufile.getbyte);
       end;
 
@@ -1462,8 +1468,15 @@
 
 
     procedure tai_label.derefimpl;
+      var
+        s : tasmsymbol;
       begin
-        objectlibrary.DerefAsmsymbol(tasmsymbol(l));
+        s:=tasmsymbol(l);
+        objectlibrary.DerefAsmsymbol(s);
+        if assigned(s) and (s is tasmlabel) then
+          l:=tasmlabel(s)
+        else
+          internalerror(2005050502);
         l.is_set:=true;
       end;
 
